Subject: [PATCH] K49: owner Send / Swap hand-off with a clear AI boundary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owners keep sovereign Send and Swap. The app only BUILDS the Safe transaction and hands off to
Safe{Wallet}. Nothing is signed or broadcast from the app, and the AI cannot send.

- Home hero: three buttons (Receive, Send, Earn) and two compact "who can do what" lines under them.
- Send sheet (ui/send/OwnerSendSheet.kt): recipient validation (40 hex, EIP-55 checksum, zero address and the
  treasury's own Safe blocked, contract and non-payee warnings, "Known payee" for an ACTIVE registered payee),
  USDC amount (<= 6 decimals, > 0), reserve check from the live WalletState buckets (amount <= Spare cash:
  green; above: red "dip by X" plus an "I understand" switch before any payload; above Safe cash: never built;
  unverified bills: "I understand" required). Output is the exact Safe tx: Base Sepolia, to = USDC token,
  value 0, operation 0 (CALL), data = transfer(recipient, amount), as copyable fields, a QR of the JSON, and
  "Open in Safe{Wallet}" (https://app.safe.global/home?safe=basesep:<Safe>). Label: "Owner-signed 2-of-2 ·
  this app holds no owner keys · the AI cannot send".
- Swap: honest hand-off. We could not confirm Safe{Wallet} swaps on Base Sepolia, so the sheet says "Swaps are not
  available on the Base Sepolia test network" and shows no quote (SwapHandoff.CONFIRMED_ON_BASE_SEPOLIA = false).
- Who can do what (Safety card + Home lines): Owner (2-of-2): Send, Swap, policy, resume. Guardian: pause, cancel
  queued. AI agent: Deposit, Withdraw, Pay verified bills, Hold, with the per-move and daily limits from the
  existing allowance formatter (allowanceCopy). DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF: Rebalance is not listed as an AI power,
  because the deployed contract reverts REBALANCE with UnsupportedAction; a footnote says so.
- CustodySplit text updated: the app now prepares a Send or Swap for the owners but never signs.
- Pure logic lives in ownersend/ (no Android UI). It encodes the transfer calldata with the existing
  Abi.addressWord / Abi.uintWord helpers. No file in ownersend/ or ui/send/ imports or calls any signer, session,
  planner or AgentRuntime class (enforced by OwnerSendBoundaryTest, which scans the real source files).

Tests: app/src/test/java/app/fusion/wallet/ownersend/ (27 tests): exact calldata bytes (expected strings computed
independently in Python; selector == keccak("transfer(address,uint256)")), EIP-55 spec vectors and the deployed
Safe/token/module addresses, recipient and amount validation, reserve verdicts on real BucketMath buckets, payload
gating (no payload until acknowledged, never above Safe cash), Safe{Wallet} link, swap honesty, role lines, and the
dependency-boundary scan (plus tests that the scanner itself catches violations).

WHAT RAN AND WHAT DID NOT (cloud session; verify on the edge before merging):
- RAN, PASSED: the 27 ownersend tests, 0 failures, compiled with Kotlin 2.0.21 on JVM 21 in a scratch Gradle JVM
